o Oka &lt;oka@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Keigo Oka &lt;oka@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Darren Krahn &lt;dkrahn@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="2" gerrit_number="351140" owner_email="oka@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="6" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/40/351140/6" remote="cros" total_fail_count="2"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="If63f9175e6e3a8e4245f6103479639dfbfe5c19d" commit="e9abab9cad201d3f8a700f5b2e438243f22f86ac" commit_message="UPSTREAM: drm/i915: Fix CHV DSI PLL refclk during state readout  Use the proper refclock frequency (100MHz) when reading out the current DSI clock on CHV.  Signed-off-by: Ville Syrjl &lt;ville.syrjala@linux.intel.com&gt; Link: http://patchwork.freedesktop.org/patch/msgid/1458052809-23426-13-git-send-email-ville.syrjala@linux.intel.com Reviewed-by: Jani Nikula &lt;jani.nikula@intel.com&gt; (cherry picked from commit ae9ec62bdadc4cd3bf893d6baced80aa3a5dbbd6 from drm-intel-next-2016-04-25) Signed-off-by: Tarun Vyas &lt;tarun.vyas@intel.com&gt;  BUG=chrome-os-partner:52640 TEST=Image builds, boots and is browse-able  Change-Id: If63f9175e6e3a8e4245f6103479639dfbfe5c19d Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/345243 Commit-Ready: Wayne Boyer &lt;wayne.boyer@intel.com&gt; Tested-by: Russ Sage &lt;russ.sage@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Stéphane Marchesin &lt;marcheu@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="2" gerrit_number="345243" owner_email="tarun.vyas@intel.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/43/345243/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="2"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ib5a902745ffa9b70860171dbbed96bcd178c69c2" commit="28dab350faf6030e1f4290833b87d3c7cf5600d4" commit_message="login: Pass ANDROID_DATA_DIR to upstart scripts.  To prepare for android-data directory migration, pass ANDROID_DATA_DIR from session_manager to upstart scripts via D-Bus signal.  BUG=b:26700652 TEST=cros_run_unit_tests --board $BOARD --packages chromeos-login TEST=Verified ANDROID_DATA_DIR is passed to upstart jobs. TEST=ARC boots.  Change-Id: Ib5a902745ffa9b70860171dbbed96bcd178c69c2 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/348128 Commit-Ready: Shuhei Takahashi &lt;nya@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Shuhei Takahashi &lt;nya@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Shuhei Takahashi &lt;nya@google.com&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="348128" owner_email="nya@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/28/348128/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ibcd998cb846cbc742601d137114b8f9416f68e41" commit="297d759c4daa9ffc8f8fca127b1722be4e55756a" commit_message="Autotest: extend the timeout limit for suite job in test push.  This CL extend the timeout limit for suite job from 24 mins to 30 mins to reduce 'timeout error' in test push.  BUG=chromium:619112 TEST=None  Change-Id: Ibcd998cb846cbc742601d137114b8f9416f68e41 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/351482 Commit-Ready: Xixuan Wu &lt;xixuan@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Xixuan Wu &lt;xixuan@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Dan Shi &lt;dshi@google.com&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="351482" owner_email="xixuan@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/82/351482/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I190a9112563fdc5ff40fa9f4ab2e03b9b7d7fa3c" commit="efeb1fbbafb4a0a963201749498447d0c5a5fdf8" commit_message="CHROMIUM: linux-firmware: Add symlink for Intel audio firmware  In the upstream linux kernel, as well as the linux-firmware git tree, the intel audio firmware is referred with the name fw_sst_0f28.bin-48kHz_i2s_master&quot; (note the 48kHz in name).  Upstream linux-firmware: 7551a3a fw_sst_0f28: Add firmware for Intel Baytrail SST DSP  Upstream linux kernel: 9b11eb4 ASoC: Intel: Update Baytrail ADSP firmware name  Yet, in our tree, this firmware is named &quot;fw_sst_0f28.bin-i2s_master&quot; (no 48kHz in name). Hence when I load 3.18 on baytrail systems, the kernel searches for, and fails to find the *48kHz* firmware file: sst-acpi 80860F28:00: Direct firmware load for intel/fw_sst_0f28.bin-48kHz_i2s_master failed with error -2  I was tempted to cherry-pick the upstream commit so that we'll have new upstream firmware image that will also have the 48kHz in name, however there are 2 issues with that:  1) Our fw image seems different than upstream (different size) and we seem to have put fixes for suspend / resume in our image. I'm not sure if the upstream version has those fixes and if we can use that.  2) We have a bunch of devices that still run older kernels (3.8/3.10) that still refer to the file as fw_sst_0f28.bin-i2s_master (no 48kHz)  This taking the simplest route so that we do not disturb any oher component - I made a symlink that points to the old firmware image - so everyone is happy.  BUG=b:28634526 TEST=On glimmer, verified that the firmware gets loaded and &quot;aplay -l&quot;      shows the audio device.  Change-Id: I190a9112563fdc5ff40fa9f4ab2e03b9b7d7fa3c Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/349343 Commit-Ready: Benson Leung &lt;bleung@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Benson Leung &lt;bleung@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Benson Leung &lt;bleung@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="2" gerrit_number="349343" owner_email="rajatja@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/linux-firmware" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/linux-firmware" ref="refs/changes/43/349343/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="2"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I58208288c0fb81228602af6f362589335b69046c" commit="c77b747158a1082dd341d5670f7d82d85c0da2d6" commit_message="Upgrade Chrome OS speech synthesis with new LSTM synthesis engine and voices  BUG=chromium:614271 TEST=manual testing using ChromeVox  Change-Id: I58208288c0fb81228602af6f362589335b69046c Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/346805 Commit-Ready: Dominic Mazzoni &lt;dmazzoni@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Dominic Mazzoni &lt;dmazzoni@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Dan Erat &lt;derat@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Dominic Mazzoni &lt;dmazzoni@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Mitsuru Oshima &lt;oshima@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: David Tseng &lt;dtseng@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="346805" owner_email="dmazzoni@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform/assets" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/assets" ref="refs/changes/05/346805/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I52968b603f0227d7d9a112b0216cd5fd6362a0b2" commit="0ac9d84d240be6496fdd0059d9ad343db0b68cb4" commit_message="tcpci: anx7688: enable message passing after hard reset sent  In TCPCI specifiction R1.0 4.7.2, the last step of transmitting hard reset message is enable PD message passing by writing to RECEIVE_MESSAGE register.  BRANCH=none BUG=chrome-os-partner:52815 TEST=manual   build and load on reference board with anx7688 port controller.   connect zinger to port 0, and use ec uart console to send hard   reset message:     pd 0 hard   check PD communication  Signed-off-by: Rong Chang &lt;rongchang@chromium.org&gt; Change-Id: I52968b603f0227d7d9a112b0216cd5fd6362a0b2 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/348142 Commit-Ready: Nicolas Boichat &lt;drinkcat@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Koro Chen &lt;koro.chen@mediatek.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Wei-Ning Huang &lt;wnhuang@chromium.org&gt; Reviewe